	"summary": {
		"text": "The Tiv are one of Nigeria’s largest peoples, over 8 million strong, and the main people of the Benue valley. Tiv is spoken mainly in Benue, and also in Taraba, Nasarawa, Plateau and Cross River. Historically the Tiv had no single monarchy; today their supreme ruler is the Tor Tiv, whose palace is in Gboko. “Munchi”, a name others once used for them, is considered offensive.",
